Minimum Toggle to Partition Difficulty: EasyAccuracy: 55.41%Submissions: 6K+Points: 2Average Time: 10m Given an array arr[] containing only 0 and 1. Find the minimum toggles (switch from 0 to 1 or vice-versa) required such the array become partitioned, i.e., it has first 0s then 1s. Examples: Input: arr = [1, 0, 1, 1, 0] Output: 2 Explaination: The changed array will be [0, 0, 1, 1, 1]. So the number of toggles here required is 2. Input: arr = [0, 1, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1] Output: 1 Explaination: The changed array will be [0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1]. Required toggles are 1. Constraints: 1 ≤ arr.size() ≤ 105 0 ≤ arr[i] ≤ 1

C++////////////

class Solution {
  public:
    int minToggle(vector<int>& arr) {
        
        int n = arr.size();
        int ones = 0;
        
        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if(arr[i] == 1)
                ones++;
        }
        
        int zeros = 0;
        int ans = n;
        
        for(int i = 0; i <= n; i++) {
            
            ans = min(ans, zeros + ones);
            
            if(i < n) {
                if(arr[i] == 0)
                    zeros++;
                else
                    ones--;
            }
        }
        
        return ans;
    }
};
